// Tyorvi's nightmare elixir: look() for shape 868.
//
// WHY THIS CLASS IS PINNED TO 868 AND CANNOT MOVE. The engine picks the
// usecode class for an item's events from its SHAPE NUMBER:
//
//     uint32 class_id = _shape;          // item.cpp:1516
//
// so shape 868's look() lands in class 868 and nowhere else, the way the
// Message Scroll's lands in 864 (MSGSCRL.UNK) and the pillars' in 865
// (ELMCOLMN.UNK). `lv_manifest.json` pins TYPEELIXIR to 868 for that
// reason. Decided by Douglas on 2026-10-09 (docs/art-track.md contract 11):
// the elixir gets its own shape and its own name.
//
// THE ITEM. Ezrekal brews it from the root and hands it over
// (lv-patched/EZREKAL.UNK, give/createNear of TypeBottle frame 0), and
// Tyorvi drinks it (lv-patched/TYORVI.UNK, the two drink filters destroy
// every TypeBottle frame 0 in the pack). TypeBottle resolves to 868 in
// u8c_symbols TYPE_SHAPES, the identifier the 1994 author used for this
// bottle at all four sites. Until 2026-10-09 it was shape 395 frame 5, the
// necromancy reagent Blood: it read "1 vial of blood" and merged with
// carried blood. Shape 868 is that vial recoloured to a sea-green brew
// (lv_art_props.py) on donor 180's TYPEFLAG row, SF_GENERIC, so it is
// neither a reagent nor a stack.
//
// THE NAME is the one the 1994 dialogue gives it: Ezrekal's menu asks "Is
// Tyorvi's elixir ready yet?" (EZREKAL.UNK). There is no German line
// because no lv-new class carries one (MSGSCRL, ELMCOLMN).

uses "item";

typeclass TypeElixir inherits Item
{
	process look();
}

process TypeElixir::look()
{
	bark("Tyorvi's elixir");
}
